{"parentUuid":"1f7f3b62-0000-4da7-8e30-5b0751b92b13","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TzwNLCShhuQ92UmbUhQm7Q","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio ESIM canister purge valve replacement youtube\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"P0456 on 2017-2023 Alfa Romeo Giulia: EVAP Small Leak Causes and Fixes\",\"url\":\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/obd-p0456-alfa-romeo-giulia-2017-2023\"},{\"title\":\"Evap Canister Replacement Alfa Romeo Giulia - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UJh89VxrVIA\"},{\"title\":\"Evap system small leak, purge valve tubing\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/evap-system-small-leak-purge-valve-tubing.59691/\"},{\"title\":\"Purge Valve - Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0L\",\"url\":\"https://shop.alfissimo.com/fuel-injection/2809-purge-valve-giuliastelvio-20l-.html\"},{\"title\":\"P0440 EVAP Fault on Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0 — FIXED! - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G9M--Poudm8\"},{\"title\":\"P2422 Evap Canister Malfunction Replacement / removal How-To\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p2422-evap-canister-malfunction-replacement-removal-how-to.63784/\"},{\"title\":\"PURGE CONTROL VALVE LOCATION REPLACEMENT EXPLAINED FIAT, ALFA ROMEO - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YfXQWoCncA4\"},{\"title\":\"P0440 CEL - Purge Valve / Solenoid Location\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p0440-cel-purge-valve-solenoid-location.64584/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo 690T engine\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_690T_engine\"},{\"title\":\"Evaporative System Integrity Module (ESIM) Replacement Tips - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=40h9LbzwVxQ\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found several relevant resources for ESIM canister and purge valve replacement on Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles:\n\n## YouTube Videos Found\n\nAn owner has documented the DIY EVAP canister replacement process on YouTube with a step-by-step guide. Specific videos include:\n\n1. **\"Evap Canister Replacement Alfa Romeo Giulia\"** - A video addressing the P2422 error code issue and EVAP valve canister replacement for trouble filling up.\n\n2. **\"P0440 EVAP Fault on Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0 — FIXED!\"** - This video demonstrates how to fix fueling issues on Giulia or Stelvio 2.0 models and includes EVAP canister replacement.\n\n3. **\"PURGE CONTROL VALVE LOCATION REPLACEMENT EXPLAINED FIAT, ALFA ROMEO\"** - A general video explaining purge control valve location and replacement for Fiat and Alfa Romeo vehicles.\n\n4. **\"Evaporative System Integrity Module (ESIM) Replacement Tips\"** - A Standard video providing tips for replacing an ESIM.\n\n## Key Information\n\nA scan tool like AlfaOBD can be used to actuate the ESIM to check for a response; a lack of clicking can indicate failure. The typical fix is to replace the entire EVAP canister assembly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d001afe8-91f0-4f22-8fe7-a3c87286863c","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:24:52.694Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio ESIM canister purge valve replacement youtube","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018EnqpgPVKwtWa8gTwepgug","content":[{"title":"P0456 on 2017-2023 Alfa Romeo Giulia: EVAP Small Leak Causes and Fixes","url":"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/obd-p0456-alfa-romeo-giulia-2017-2023"},{"title":"Evap Canister Replacement Alfa Romeo Giulia - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UJh89VxrVIA"},{"title":"Evap system small leak, purge valve tubing","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/evap-system-small-leak-purge-valve-tubing.59691/"},{"title":"Purge Valve - Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0L","url":"https://shop.alfissimo.com/fuel-injection/2809-purge-valve-giuliastelvio-20l-.html"},{"title":"P0440 EVAP Fault on Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0 — FIXED! - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G9M--Poudm8"},{"title":"P2422 Evap Canister Malfunction Replacement / removal How-To","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p2422-evap-canister-malfunction-replacement-removal-how-to.63784/"},{"title":"PURGE CONTROL VALVE LOCATION REPLACEMENT EXPLAINED FIAT, ALFA ROMEO - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YfXQWoCncA4"},{"title":"P0440 CEL - Purge Valve / Solenoid Location","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p0440-cel-purge-valve-solenoid-location.64584/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo 690T engine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_690T_engine"},{"title":"Evaporative System Integrity Module (ESIM) Replacement Tips - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=40h9LbzwVxQ"}]},"Based on the web search results, I found several relevant resources for ESIM canister and purge valve replacement on Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles:\n\n## YouTube Videos Found\n\nAn owner has documented the DIY EVAP canister replacement process on YouTube with a step-by-step guide. Specific videos include:\n\n1. **\"Evap Canister Replacement Alfa Romeo Giulia\"** - A video addressing the P2422 error code issue and EVAP valve canister replacement for trouble filling up.\n\n2. **\"P0440 EVAP Fault on Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0 — FIXED!\"** - This video demonstrates how to fix fueling issues on Giulia or Stelvio 2.0 models and includes EVAP canister replacement.\n\n3. **\"PURGE CONTROL VALVE LOCATION REPLACEMENT EXPLAINED FIAT, ALFA ROMEO\"** - A general video explaining purge control valve location and replacement for Fiat and Alfa Romeo vehicles.\n\n4. **\"Evaporative System Integrity Module (ESIM) Replacement Tips\"** - A Standard video providing tips for replacing an ESIM.\n\n## Key Information\n\nA scan tool like AlfaOBD can be used to actuate the ESIM to check for a response; a lack of clicking can indicate failure. The typical fix is to replace the entire EVAP canister assembly."],"durationSeconds":6.3034011000394825,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b2722a4-8395-41f7-bb5e-53fb210be1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1f7f3b62-0000-4da7-8e30-5b0751b92b13","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"adcf5f46-725b-4aef-b8c1-c70389279a92","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KeH3efk6X2aiPEz67BiHHE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Giorgio platform U0100 U0073 network cascade battery ground Alfa Romeo forum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FCA Giorgio platform\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FCA_Giorgio_platform\"},{\"title\":\"About: FCA Giorgio platform\",\"url\":\"https://dbpedia.org/page/FCA_Giorgio_platform\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo to ditch Giorgio platform in favor of Stellantis' new electrified designs\",\"url\":\"https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1132028_alfa-romeo-to-ditch-giorgio-platform-in-favor-of-stellantis-new-electrified-designs\"},{\"title\":\"No Start - U0100 Error\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/no-start-u0100-error.50241/\"},{\"title\":\"This is the new Giorgio EV platform.\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/this-is-the-new-giorgio-ev-platform.20332/\"},{\"title\":\"Battery ground?\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfabb.com/threads/battery-ground.272562/\"},{\"title\":\"Check engine light - fault code U0100\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/check-engine-light-fault-code-u0100.1071346/\"},{\"title\":\"Fiat Premium platform\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Motors/Fiat_Premium_platform\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"}]\n\nI found some relevant search results for your query. Here's what I discovered:\n\n**Giorgio Platform Overview:**\nThe FCA Giorgio Platform is an automobile platform made by Alfa Romeo since 2015, debuting in the Alfa Romeo Giulia. The Stelvio uses the same Giorgio platform already used by the Giulia.\n\n**U0100 Error Code - Network Communication:**\nThe search results include forum discussions about the U0100 error code on Alfa Romeo vehicles. This is an ECM communications error, and U0100 is a nice generic message indicating a loss of communications between the systems. The first step on this is always check battery.\n\n**Battery and Ground Issues:**\nForum discussions mention battery-related concerns and grounding. There should be an 8 x 1.25 nutplate in the front panel by the battery, for the ground.\n\nThe search results show discussions from Alfa Romeo forums (giuliaforums.com, alfaowner.com) addressing U0100 errors in context of battery voltage and network communication issues, which aligns with your search query about network cascade, battery ground issues on the Giorgio platform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"040614ac-ed14-436e-a430-e70804f71325","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:24:53.506Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Giorgio platform U0100 U0073 network cascade battery ground Alfa Romeo forum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HU129CmyZsV2XMQAYqAWzD","content":[{"title":"FCA Giorgio platform","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FCA_Giorgio_platform"},{"title":"About: FCA Giorgio platform","url":"https://dbpedia.org/page/FCA_Giorgio_platform"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo to ditch Giorgio platform in favor of Stellantis' new electrified designs","url":"https://www.motorauthority.com/news/1132028_alfa-romeo-to-ditch-giorgio-platform-in-favor-of-stellantis-new-electrified-designs"},{"title":"No Start - U0100 Error","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/no-start-u0100-error.50241/"},{"title":"This is the new Giorgio EV platform.","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/this-is-the-new-giorgio-ev-platform.20332/"},{"title":"Battery ground?","url":"https://www.alfabb.com/threads/battery-ground.272562/"},{"title":"Check engine light - fault code U0100","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/check-engine-light-fault-code-u0100.1071346/"},{"title":"Fiat Premium platform","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Motors/Fiat_Premium_platform"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"}]},"I found some relevant search results for your query. Here's what I discovered:\n\n**Giorgio Platform Overview:**\nThe FCA Giorgio Platform is an automobile platform made by Alfa Romeo since 2015, debuting in the Alfa Romeo Giulia. The Stelvio uses the same Giorgio platform already used by the Giulia.\n\n**U0100 Error Code - Network Communication:**\nThe search results include forum discussions about the U0100 error code on Alfa Romeo vehicles. This is an ECM communications error, and U0100 is a nice generic message indicating a loss of communications between the systems. The first step on this is always check battery.\n\n**Battery and Ground Issues:**\nForum discussions mention battery-related concerns and grounding. There should be an 8 x 1.25 nutplate in the front panel by the battery, for the ground.\n\nThe search results show discussions from Alfa Romeo forums (giuliaforums.com, alfaowner.com) addressing U0100 errors in context of battery voltage and network communication issues, which aligns with your search query about network cascade, battery ground issues on the Giorgio platform."],"durationSeconds":6.476988699913025,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b2722a4-8395-41f7-bb5e-53fb210be1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"adcf5f46-725b-4aef-b8c1-c70389279a92","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"614fbbf7-a457-4aa7-87fe-f0688223e3fa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J6Q7k6i29pUcKgydkB7a98","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"P0455 P0456 Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio EVAP forum thread stelvioforum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Code P0456 on a 2019 Quadrifoglio\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/code-p0456-on-a-2019-quadrifoglio.19288/\"},{\"title\":\"PO440 EVAP Failure (error Code)\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/po440-evap-failure-error-code.59740/\"},{\"title\":\"2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio EVAP Canister/EVAP Leak Sensor - P0440 and P0456\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/2018-alfa-romeo-stelvio-evap-canister-evap-leak-sensor-p0440-and-p0456.24981/\"},{\"title\":\"How many different Vapor Canister P/Ns are there?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/how-many-different-vapor-canister-p-ns-are-there.22360/\"},{\"title\":\"P0456\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p0456.51472/\"},{\"title\":\"Squadra Logger Reading Codes (P219C, P0455, P0457) - No real issues but question for the group?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/squadra-logger-reading-codes-p219c-p0455-p0457-no-real-issues-but-question-for-the-group.22705/\"},{\"title\":\"P0455 evaporative emission system large leak detected for the umpteenth time\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p0455-evaporative-emission-system-large-leak-detected-for-the-umpteenth-time.58868/\"},{\"title\":\"P0456 small leak in evap system help\",\"url\":\"https://www.4c-forums.com/threads/p0456-small-leak-in-evap-system-help.69234/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"},{\"title\":\"So you have an evap code (p0455, p0442)...\",\"url\":\"https://www.dodgetalk.com/threads/so-you-have-an-evap-code-p0455-p0442.256169/\"}]\n\nI found several forum threads related to P0455 and P0456 EVAP codes on Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here are the relevant results:\n\n## Stelvio Forum Threads:\n\n1. **Code P0456 on a 2019 Quadrifoglio** - A user reported dealing with a recurring P0456 \"Evaporative Emission System Leak Detected (very small leak)\" code. The car drives normally with the exception of being locked out of any drive mode other than \"Normal\".\n\n2. **2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio EVAP Canister/EVAP Leak Sensor - P0440 and P0456** - A user noted that the EVAP leak detection pump can cause the P0456 small EVAP leak code, and they found the old O-ring on this pump was in poor condition.\n\n3. **How many different Vapor Canister P/Ns are there?** - A user working on a P0456 very small leak problem found at least 4 different part numbers for vapor canisters.\n\n4. **Squadra Logger Reading Codes (P219C, P0455, P0457)** - A user reported these codes appearing with a Squadra Logger after the car had been in for service for evap system leak.\n\n## Giulia Forums:\n\n**P0455 evaporative emission system large leak detected** - A user reported P0455 errors recurring every few weeks despite canister replacement.\n\nThese threads discuss various potential causes including gas cap issues, vapor canister failures, EVAP leak detection pump problems, and purge valve issues.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ca2f31b6-1973-4f24-86fe-fcfebbd3c081","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:24:53.618Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"P0455 P0456 Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio EVAP forum thread stelvioforum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015LL14VSReM2J5pYyAkZoXc","content":[{"title":"Code P0456 on a 2019 Quadrifoglio","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/code-p0456-on-a-2019-quadrifoglio.19288/"},{"title":"PO440 EVAP Failure (error Code)","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/po440-evap-failure-error-code.59740/"},{"title":"2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio EVAP Canister/EVAP Leak Sensor - P0440 and P0456","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/2018-alfa-romeo-stelvio-evap-canister-evap-leak-sensor-p0440-and-p0456.24981/"},{"title":"How many different Vapor Canister P/Ns are there?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/how-many-different-vapor-canister-p-ns-are-there.22360/"},{"title":"P0456","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p0456.51472/"},{"title":"Squadra Logger Reading Codes (P219C, P0455, P0457) - No real issues but question for the group?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/squadra-logger-reading-codes-p219c-p0455-p0457-no-real-issues-but-question-for-the-group.22705/"},{"title":"P0455 evaporative emission system large leak detected for the umpteenth time","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/p0455-evaporative-emission-system-large-leak-detected-for-the-umpteenth-time.58868/"},{"title":"P0456 small leak in evap system help","url":"https://www.4c-forums.com/threads/p0456-small-leak-in-evap-system-help.69234/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"},{"title":"So you have an evap code (p0455, p0442)...","url":"https://www.dodgetalk.com/threads/so-you-have-an-evap-code-p0455-p0442.256169/"}]},"I found several forum threads related to P0455 and P0456 EVAP codes on Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here are the relevant results:\n\n## Stelvio Forum Threads:\n\n1. **Code P0456 on a 2019 Quadrifoglio** - A user reported dealing with a recurring P0456 \"Evaporative Emission System Leak Detected (very small leak)\" code. The car drives normally with the exception of being locked out of any drive mode other than \"Normal\".\n\n2. **2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio EVAP Canister/EVAP Leak Sensor - P0440 and P0456** - A user noted that the EVAP leak detection pump can cause the P0456 small EVAP leak code, and they found the old O-ring on this pump was in poor condition.\n\n3. **How many different Vapor Canister P/Ns are there?** - A user working on a P0456 very small leak problem found at least 4 different part numbers for vapor canisters.\n\n4. **Squadra Logger Reading Codes (P219C, P0455, P0457)** - A user reported these codes appearing with a Squadra Logger after the car had been in for service for evap system leak.\n\n## Giulia Forums:\n\n**P0455 evaporative emission system large leak detected** - A user reported P0455 errors recurring every few weeks despite canister replacement.\n\nThese threads discuss various potential causes including gas cap issues, vapor canister failures, EVAP leak detection pump problems, and purge valve issues."],"durationSeconds":7.843396800041199,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b2722a4-8395-41f7-bb5e-53fb210be1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"614fbbf7-a457-4aa7-87fe-f0688223e3fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2ad130a0-398c-447a-ba01-7e0eddc7ec03","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NeuADDbSUSaEhsa4NDKUp6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"B1176 window initialization Alfa Giulia Stelvio forum fix\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MES Functions\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/mes-functions.21770/\"},{\"title\":\"Sunroof Reset?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/sunroof-reset.17845/\"},{\"title\":\"Software update\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/software-update.21608/\"},{\"title\":\"Blank infotainment screen\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/blank-infotainment-screen.39138/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"},{\"title\":\"How to: Infotainment updates\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/how-to-infotainment-updates.1185573/\"},{\"title\":\"Remote Window Up/Down\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/remote-window-up-down.6497/\"},{\"title\":\"Remote windows up/down\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/remote-windows-up-down.39378/\"},{\"title\":\"Infotainment System off (black screen) when start car\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/infotainment-system-off-black-screen-when-start-car.17425/\"},{\"title\":\"Infotainment Screen Blank\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/infotainment-screen-blank.56806/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about window initialization for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles:\n\nThe comfort windows function allows you to use the key fob to close/open all windows, and after enabling it you need to re-initialize windows for it to work. \n\nHowever, there are some important limitations: The window function won't work when the car is set to US settings, and if you change it to a Euro country setting, some things may stop working due to different electronics/modules in North American spec'd cars, with speculation that Alfa Romeo didn't allow this in NA cars because of potential legal issues.\n\nThe search results also mention re-initialization procedures for automatic sunroof operation in case of faulty operation, which may also be necessary after the vehicle's battery has been disconnected and then reconnected, noting that the anti-pinch safety device is deactivated during the re-initialization procedure.\n\nThe specific error code \"B1176\" didn't appear in these forum results, so I wasn't able to find detailed information about what that particular error code refers to or specific fixes for it. You may want to search for B1176 error code specifically or check technical documentation for more details on that code.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cb39916c-5303-4b19-ba27-b08944600aaa","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:24:53.804Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"B1176 window initialization Alfa Giulia Stelvio forum fix","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013CxhK6FeYKcK5rw4B3Mx1u","content":[{"title":"MES Functions","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/mes-functions.21770/"},{"title":"Sunroof Reset?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/sunroof-reset.17845/"},{"title":"Software update","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/software-update.21608/"},{"title":"Blank infotainment screen","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/blank-infotainment-screen.39138/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"},{"title":"How to: Infotainment updates","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/how-to-infotainment-updates.1185573/"},{"title":"Remote Window Up/Down","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/remote-window-up-down.6497/"},{"title":"Remote windows up/down","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/remote-windows-up-down.39378/"},{"title":"Infotainment System off (black screen) when start car","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/infotainment-system-off-black-screen-when-start-car.17425/"},{"title":"Infotainment Screen Blank","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/infotainment-screen-blank.56806/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about window initialization for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles:\n\nThe comfort windows function allows you to use the key fob to close/open all windows, and after enabling it you need to re-initialize windows for it to work. \n\nHowever, there are some important limitations: The window function won't work when the car is set to US settings, and if you change it to a Euro country setting, some things may stop working due to different electronics/modules in North American spec'd cars, with speculation that Alfa Romeo didn't allow this in NA cars because of potential legal issues.\n\nThe search results also mention re-initialization procedures for automatic sunroof operation in case of faulty operation, which may also be necessary after the vehicle's battery has been disconnected and then reconnected, noting that the anti-pinch safety device is deactivated during the re-initialization procedure.\n\nThe specific error code \"B1176\" didn't appear in these forum results, so I wasn't able to find detailed information about what that particular error code refers to or specific fixes for it. You may want to search for B1176 error code specifically or check technical documentation for more details on that code."],"durationSeconds":6.223515100002289,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b2722a4-8395-41f7-bb5e-53fb210be1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2ad130a0-398c-447a-ba01-7e0eddc7ec03","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"d732510e-d851-427e-a47e-dbe63b11a810","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RJPGNQ9jwmmbrVWMoi5tBS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"C141B C141C Alfa Romeo Stelvio camera radar code forum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NUMBER: 08-045-20 REV. A GROUP: 08 - Electrical DATE: August 18, 2020\",\"url\":\"https://static.nhtsa.gov/odi/tsbs/2020/MC-10180265-9999.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Odometer blinking, DNA not working, C-1408-86 (ESC), C141C-86 (camera), U0102-00 (AWD0 failure\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/odometer-blinking-dna-not-working-c-1408-86-esc-c141c-86-camera-u0102-00-awd0-failure.24275/\"},{\"title\":\"(UK) Stelvio Multi Air Filter Replacement Under Warranty\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/uk-stelvio-multi-air-filter-replacement-under-warranty.23508/\"},{\"title\":\"FCW limited functionality check front camera [SOLVED]\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/fcw-limited-functionality-check-front-camera-solved.1206089/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Radar Calibration\",\"url\":\"https://diag.net/msg/mylfenr4v8hnm0ss7sg1ling13\"},{\"title\":\"ACC -> \\\"dumb\\\" CC switch?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/acc-dumb-cc-switch.17597/\"},{\"title\":\"C41\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C41\"},{\"title\":\"Can a second hand front radar be coded to my car\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/can-a-second-hand-front-radar-be-coded-to-my-car.1205535/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Definition, Causes and Diagnosis\",\"url\":\"https://www.dtcdecode.com/Alfa-Romeo\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Cruise control ACC installation\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/adaptive-cruise-control-acc-installation.10547/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about these diagnostic trouble codes for the Alfa Romeo Stelvio:\n\n## Code Definitions\n\nC141B-97 is a video camera blind code indicating component or system operation obstructed or blocked, while C141C-86 is a Video Camera Private Can Communication Failure - Signal Invalid.\n\n## Discussion Forum Context\n\nThese codes have been discussed in Alfa Romeo owner forums, particularly the Stelvio Forum. Users have reported seeing C141C-86 alongside other errors like C1408-86 (ESC Fail Status) and U0102-00 (Lost Communication With Transfer Case Control Module).\n\n## Troubleshooting Attempts\n\nUsers scanning with diagnostic tools have gotten the code C141C-86 described as \"Private CAN between HALF and DASM\" and have tried disconnecting/reconnecting the front camera and performing proxy alignment without immediate success. In at least one case, replacing the front camera resolved the error code.\n\nThese codes are related to the forward collision warning (FCW) and adaptive cruise control (ACC) systems on the Stelvio, which rely on both camera and radar sensors functioning properly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3e79fb00-e249-4583-bcd8-58f72a777bcf","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:24:54.184Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"C141B C141C Alfa Romeo Stelvio camera radar code forum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KB6MwgBL5oRupkuyK5Bdme","content":[{"title":"NUMBER: 08-045-20 REV. A GROUP: 08 - Electrical DATE: August 18, 2020","url":"https://static.nhtsa.gov/odi/tsbs/2020/MC-10180265-9999.pdf"},{"title":"Odometer blinking, DNA not working, C-1408-86 (ESC), C141C-86 (camera), U0102-00 (AWD0 failure","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/odometer-blinking-dna-not-working-c-1408-86-esc-c141c-86-camera-u0102-00-awd0-failure.24275/"},{"title":"(UK) Stelvio Multi Air Filter Replacement Under Warranty","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/uk-stelvio-multi-air-filter-replacement-under-warranty.23508/"},{"title":"FCW limited functionality check front camera [SOLVED]","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/fcw-limited-functionality-check-front-camera-solved.1206089/"},{"title":"Alfa Radar Calibration","url":"https://diag.net/msg/mylfenr4v8hnm0ss7sg1ling13"},{"title":"ACC -> \"dumb\" CC switch?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/acc-dumb-cc-switch.17597/"},{"title":"C41","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C41"},{"title":"Can a second hand front radar be coded to my car","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/can-a-second-hand-front-radar-be-coded-to-my-car.1205535/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) Definition, Causes and Diagnosis","url":"https://www.dtcdecode.com/Alfa-Romeo"},{"title":"Adaptive Cruise control ACC installation","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/adaptive-cruise-control-acc-installation.10547/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about these diagnostic trouble codes for the Alfa Romeo Stelvio:\n\n## Code Definitions\n\nC141B-97 is a video camera blind code indicating component or system operation obstructed or blocked, while C141C-86 is a Video Camera Private Can Communication Failure - Signal Invalid.\n\n## Discussion Forum Context\n\nThese codes have been discussed in Alfa Romeo owner forums, particularly the Stelvio Forum. Users have reported seeing C141C-86 alongside other errors like C1408-86 (ESC Fail Status) and U0102-00 (Lost Communication With Transfer Case Control Module).\n\n## Troubleshooting Attempts\n\nUsers scanning with diagnostic tools have gotten the code C141C-86 described as \"Private CAN between HALF and DASM\" and have tried disconnecting/reconnecting the front camera and performing proxy alignment without immediate success. In at least one case, replacing the front camera resolved the error code.\n\nThese codes are related to the forward collision warning (FCW) and adaptive cruise control (ACC) systems on the Stelvio, which rely on both camera and radar sensors functioning properly."],"durationSeconds":6.087266200065613,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b2722a4-8395-41f7-bb5e-53fb210be1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d732510e-d851-427e-a47e-dbe63b11a810","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"8b3ebd9a-e870-42ee-9adf-44c49aafb716","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HNK9HMe1gbsGqbYZLKA8bs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo 2.0T misfire P0300 coil pack spark plug youtube replacement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"misfire nightmare\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/misfire-nightmare.14576/\"},{\"title\":\"Fault codes P0300 and p0301\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/fault-codes-p0300-and-p0301.525865/\"},{\"title\":\"Code P0300 - Multiple Cylinder Misfire (2017 Giulia Ti)\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/code-p0300-multiple-cylinder-misfire-2017-giulia-ti.64580/\"},{\"title\":\"P0300 Code Guide: Diagnosis, Causes & Fixes\",\"url\":\"https://www.identifix.com/blogs/p0300-code-the-guide-to-diagnostics-and-repair/\"},{\"title\":\"How To Fix An Engine Misfire-P0300 (Bad Ignition Coil) - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6icmfICvyp0\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo P0300 Random Cylinder Misfire Condition\",\"url\":\"https://www.carobdcodes.com/alfa-romeo-p0300-random-cylinder-misfire-condition.shtml\"},{\"title\":\"Fault Code P0300 Misfire: How to Fix it Yourself (2026)\",\"url\":\"https://uk.haynes.com/blogs/tips-tutorials/how-to-fix-fault-code-p0300\"},{\"title\":\"P0300 — Meaning, Causes & Fix (Expert-Reviewed)\",\"url\":\"https://obdadvisor.com/codes/p0300/\"},{\"title\":\"P0300 Code: Random or Multiple Cylinder Misfire Detected - In The Garage with CarParts.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.carparts.com/blog/p0300-code-random-or-multiple-cylinder-misfire-detected/\"},{\"title\":\"Confirm this item fits\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.com/itm/291237399026\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Alfa Romeo 2.0T misfire issues with the P0300 code:\n\n## What P0300 Means\n\nThe P0300 code indicates that the car's computer has detected that not all of the engine's cylinders are firing properly, representing a random or multiple misfire.\n\n## Common Causes for Alfa Romeo\n\nFor Alfa Romeo vehicles, possible causes of P0300 include faulty spark plugs or wires, faulty coil packs, faulty oxygen sensors, faulty fuel injectors, burned exhaust valves, faulty catalytic converters, stuck/blocked EGR valves, faulty camshaft position sensors, and defective computers.\n\n## Diagnostic Approach\n\nIf you suspect a specific coil, you can swap it with one from a known-good cylinder, clear the codes and drive. If the misfire follows the coil to the new cylinder, you've confirmed the bad coil. If it stays, the problem is in the original cylinder (injector, compression, etc.).\n\n## Common Fixes\n\nThe most common fix is worn spark plugs or coils. If the cause is determined to be worn spark plugs or a faulty ignition coil, these will need to be replaced. If the cause is a clogged fuel injector, it too will need to be replaced.\n\nThe search results also included a YouTube video link (result #5) that shows a P0300 misfire repair in real-time, which may be helpful for visual guidance on the replacement process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8ca0e907-b763-40d8-821f-270b8486b381","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:24:55.035Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo 2.0T misfire P0300 coil pack spark plug youtube replacement","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01YAY4QaiEj6QKpTwdbmNrSZ","content":[{"title":"misfire nightmare","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/misfire-nightmare.14576/"},{"title":"Fault codes P0300 and p0301","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/fault-codes-p0300-and-p0301.525865/"},{"title":"Code P0300 - Multiple Cylinder Misfire (2017 Giulia Ti)","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/code-p0300-multiple-cylinder-misfire-2017-giulia-ti.64580/"},{"title":"P0300 Code Guide: Diagnosis, Causes & Fixes","url":"https://www.identifix.com/blogs/p0300-code-the-guide-to-diagnostics-and-repair/"},{"title":"How To Fix An Engine Misfire-P0300 (Bad Ignition Coil) - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6icmfICvyp0"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo P0300 Random Cylinder Misfire Condition","url":"https://www.carobdcodes.com/alfa-romeo-p0300-random-cylinder-misfire-condition.shtml"},{"title":"Fault Code P0300 Misfire: How to Fix it Yourself (2026)","url":"https://uk.haynes.com/blogs/tips-tutorials/how-to-fix-fault-code-p0300"},{"title":"P0300 — Meaning, Causes & Fix (Expert-Reviewed)","url":"https://obdadvisor.com/codes/p0300/"},{"title":"P0300 Code: Random or Multiple Cylinder Misfire Detected - In The Garage with CarParts.com","url":"https://www.carparts.com/blog/p0300-code-random-or-multiple-cylinder-misfire-detected/"},{"title":"Confirm this item fits","url":"https://www.ebay.com/itm/291237399026"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about Alfa Romeo 2.0T misfire issues with the P0300 code:\n\n## What P0300 Means\n\nThe P0300 code indicates that the car's computer has detected that not all of the engine's cylinders are firing properly, representing a random or multiple misfire.\n\n## Common Causes for Alfa Romeo\n\nFor Alfa Romeo vehicles, possible causes of P0300 include faulty spark plugs or wires, faulty coil packs, faulty oxygen sensors, faulty fuel injectors, burned exhaust valves, faulty catalytic converters, stuck/blocked EGR valves, faulty camshaft position sensors, and defective computers.\n\n## Diagnostic Approach\n\nIf you suspect a specific coil, you can swap it with one from a known-good cylinder, clear the codes and drive. If the misfire follows the coil to the new cylinder, you've confirmed the bad coil. If it stays, the problem is in the original cylinder (injector, compression, etc.).\n\n## Common Fixes\n\nThe most common fix is worn spark plugs or coils. If the cause is determined to be worn spark plugs or a faulty ignition coil, these will need to be replaced. If the cause is a clogged fuel injector, it too will need to be replaced.\n\nThe search results also included a YouTube video link (result #5) that shows a P0300 misfire repair in real-time, which may be helpful for visual guidance on the replacement process."],"durationSeconds":6.499235199928283,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8b2722a4-8395-41f7-bb5e-53fb210be1d0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8b3ebd9a-e870-42ee-9adf-44c49aafb716","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
