{"parentUuid":"075f77ff-81c4-43d7-a528-ee69f2a130d8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sy5ihjDRrok54cBWSNDE8h","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio engine air filter cabin air filter replacement youtube\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Cabin Air Filter\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/cabin-air-filter.8687/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio HVAC Cabin Filter Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=QmrlOwPSvYQ\"},{\"title\":\"Got my cabin air filter replaced\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/got-my-cabin-air-filter-replaced.66541/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio cabin air filter replacement - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sGRjlOnN8rM\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio EASY Cabin Filter Replacement DIY - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JlLFoTKQ-nY\"},{\"title\":\"How To Replace Air Filter In Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia Quadrifoglio - Step By Step - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KxBRCCChQp0\"},{\"title\":\"[guide] cabin air filter replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/guide-cabin-air-filter-replacement.63868/\"},{\"title\":\"Cabin/Pollen Filter location and replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/cabin-pollen-filter-location-and-replacement.28249/\"},{\"title\":\"How to change the Air filter change Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2018 🔧step by step🔧 - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-0aPue_mjHw\"},{\"title\":\"Quick & Easy Guide: Changing the Air Filter on Your Alfa Romeo Giulia - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GgePKewmUkY\"}]\n\nThe search has returned several useful results about air filter and cabin air filter replacement for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here are the key findings:\n\n**Cabin Air Filter Replacement:**\nThe cabin air filter on the Giulia and Stelvio are both located on the right side of the vehicle. You need to take off the passenger footwell panel, remove a small metal brace, and a hard-to-reach screw for the filter box door, then pop it off and pull out the filter.\n\n**YouTube Resources:**\nSeveral step-by-step YouTube tutorials are available:\n- \"Alfa Romeo Stelvio HVAC Cabin Filter Replacement Step By Step DIY\"\n- \"Step by step instructions for the terribly designed cabin air filter replacement for the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio\"\n- A step-by-step tutorial for cabin air filter replacement\n- \"How To Replace Air Filter In Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia Quadrifoglio - Step By Step\"\n- A video showing how to change the air filter on your Alfa Romeo Giulia quickly and easily\n\n**Engine Air Filter:**\nA tutorial showing how to remove the old engine air filter, install the new one correctly using basic tools is also available on YouTube.\n\nThe search results indicate that multiple YouTube tutorials exist for both cabin and engine air filter replacements for these vehicles.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"32472bc2-b3a8-4b5a-886a-8175abb143d4","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:09.636Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio engine air filter cabin air filter replacement youtube","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QUQMe8fiGrHssD64tVSWQY","content":[{"title":"Cabin Air Filter","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/cabin-air-filter.8687/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio HVAC Cabin Filter Replacement","url":"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=QmrlOwPSvYQ"},{"title":"Got my cabin air filter replaced","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/got-my-cabin-air-filter-replaced.66541/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio cabin air filter replacement - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sGRjlOnN8rM"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio EASY Cabin Filter Replacement DIY - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JlLFoTKQ-nY"},{"title":"How To Replace Air Filter In Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia Quadrifoglio - Step By Step - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KxBRCCChQp0"},{"title":"[guide] cabin air filter replacement","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/guide-cabin-air-filter-replacement.63868/"},{"title":"Cabin/Pollen Filter location and replacement","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/cabin-pollen-filter-location-and-replacement.28249/"},{"title":"How to change the Air filter change Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2018 🔧step by step🔧 - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-0aPue_mjHw"},{"title":"Quick & Easy Guide: Changing the Air Filter on Your Alfa Romeo Giulia - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GgePKewmUkY"}]},"The search has returned several useful results about air filter and cabin air filter replacement for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here are the key findings:\n\n**Cabin Air Filter Replacement:**\nThe cabin air filter on the Giulia and Stelvio are both located on the right side of the vehicle. You need to take off the passenger footwell panel, remove a small metal brace, and a hard-to-reach screw for the filter box door, then pop it off and pull out the filter.\n\n**YouTube Resources:**\nSeveral step-by-step YouTube tutorials are available:\n- \"Alfa Romeo Stelvio HVAC Cabin Filter Replacement Step By Step DIY\"\n- \"Step by step instructions for the terribly designed cabin air filter replacement for the 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio\"\n- A step-by-step tutorial for cabin air filter replacement\n- \"How To Replace Air Filter In Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia Quadrifoglio - Step By Step\"\n- A video showing how to change the air filter on your Alfa Romeo Giulia quickly and easily\n\n**Engine Air Filter:**\nA tutorial showing how to remove the old engine air filter, install the new one correctly using basic tools is also available on YouTube.\n\nThe search results indicate that multiple YouTube tutorials exist for both cabin and engine air filter replacements for these vehicles."],"durationSeconds":5.97665130007267,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"075f77ff-81c4-43d7-a528-ee69f2a130d8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"600913f1-42a8-4ce2-8362-47ab92afdafa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tv67Gu1f7agwnVCZJ7xYnC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo 2.0T drive belt serpentine belt replacement youtube\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio serpentine belt replacement 2.0L engine - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1B4eVCVzZc\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T Serpentine Belt Change - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T9ocCL2jNzQ\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia DIY Serpentine belt replacement - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xUhkPMQcoS8\"},{\"title\":\"Timing Belt Replacement on Alfa Romeo GT 2.0 JTS — With an Unexpected Surprise! - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/d3SMyNl3MZA\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0 Auxiliary Belt Replacement - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CWT8N9NaxnA\"},{\"title\":\"Serpentine Belt Group Service\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/serpentine-belt-group-service.63974/\"},{\"title\":\"Aux Drive Belt Giulia Stelvio 2.0T\",\"url\":\"https://centerlinealfa.com/catalog/aux-drive-belt-giulia-stelvio-20t\"},{\"title\":\"30K Service Serpentine Belt 2.0 Engine\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/30k-service-serpentine-belt-2-0-engine.10697/\"},{\"title\":\"Video of Serpentine Belt access\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/video-of-serpentine-belt-access.68172/\"},{\"title\":\"Bestätigen, dass das Teil passt\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/134639424603\"}]\n\nI found several YouTube videos and resources for Alfa Romeo 2.0T serpentine belt replacement:\n\n**YouTube Videos:**\n\n1. Alfa Romeo Stelvio serpentine belt replacement with step-by-step instructions for the 2.0L turbocharged engine - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1B4eVCVzZc\n\n2. Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T Serpentine Belt Change with step-by-step accessory belt replacement guide - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T9ocCL2jNzQ\n\n3. Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia DIY Serpentine belt replacement guide for the 2.0 engine - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xUhkPMQcoS8\n\n4. Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0 Auxiliary Belt Replacement video - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CWT8N9NaxnA\n\nThese videos cover the 2.0T turbocharged engines found in both Giulia and Stelvio models, and provide visual step-by-step guidance for the replacement process.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3ca3ade5-e348-40a6-ab2f-89a8c4f55018","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:11.436Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo 2.0T drive belt serpentine belt replacement youtube","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01K3MrakwYcrdL3QZNqEwHco","content":[{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio serpentine belt replacement 2.0L engine - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1B4eVCVzZc"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T Serpentine Belt Change - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T9ocCL2jNzQ"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia DIY Serpentine belt replacement - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xUhkPMQcoS8"},{"title":"Timing Belt Replacement on Alfa Romeo GT 2.0 JTS — With an Unexpected Surprise! - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/d3SMyNl3MZA"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0 Auxiliary Belt Replacement - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CWT8N9NaxnA"},{"title":"Serpentine Belt Group Service","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/serpentine-belt-group-service.63974/"},{"title":"Aux Drive Belt Giulia Stelvio 2.0T","url":"https://centerlinealfa.com/catalog/aux-drive-belt-giulia-stelvio-20t"},{"title":"30K Service Serpentine Belt 2.0 Engine","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/30k-service-serpentine-belt-2-0-engine.10697/"},{"title":"Video of Serpentine Belt access","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/video-of-serpentine-belt-access.68172/"},{"title":"Bestätigen, dass das Teil passt","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/134639424603"}]},"I found several YouTube videos and resources for Alfa Romeo 2.0T serpentine belt replacement:\n\n**YouTube Videos:**\n\n1. Alfa Romeo Stelvio serpentine belt replacement with step-by-step instructions for the 2.0L turbocharged engine - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u1B4eVCVzZc\n\n2. Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0T Serpentine Belt Change with step-by-step accessory belt replacement guide - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T9ocCL2jNzQ\n\n3. Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia DIY Serpentine belt replacement guide for the 2.0 engine - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xUhkPMQcoS8\n\n4. Alfa Romeo Giulia/Stelvio 2.0 Auxiliary Belt Replacement video - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CWT8N9NaxnA\n\nThese videos cover the 2.0T turbocharged engines found in both Giulia and Stelvio models, and provide visual step-by-step guidance for the replacement process."],"durationSeconds":6.05842509996891,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"600913f1-42a8-4ce2-8362-47ab92afdafa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"ae332e35-71f5-4720-baf7-5a627777db3b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TdT76Cct27AMgG2ocyEcah","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio brake fluid flush EPB service mode youtube\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2018-2022 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0 brake fluid flush service - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLftfWIJIWQ\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia Quadrifoglio Brake Service Mode and Replacement- Step-By-Step - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VHTnQ6o1fNE\"},{\"title\":\"Brakes stuck in service mode!\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/brakes-stuck-in-service-mode.20545/\"},{\"title\":\"Brake fluid flush\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-fluid-flush.42916/\"},{\"title\":\"Brake fluid change\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-fluid-change.63954/\"},{\"title\":\"Brake Flush Requirements and Questions\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-flush-requirements-and-questions.65821/\"},{\"title\":\"How to release stuck E-brake in Brake Service Mode\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-release-stuck-e-brake-in-brake-service-mode.50188/\"},{\"title\":\"When to replace brake fluid?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/when-to-replace-brake-fluid.18250/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Put the Electronic Parking Brake into Service Mode on a Alfa Romeo Stelvio (2017–present)\",\"url\":\"https://servicereset.net/maintenance/alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-present-epb-service-mode/\"},{\"title\":\"Has anyone had a break fluid change done?\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/has-anyone-had-a-break-fluid-change-done.44588/\"}]\n\nI found several relevant results for your search about Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio brake fluid flush and EPB service mode:\n\n## YouTube Videos\n\nThere is a step-by-step YouTube video that provides instructions on how to perform a brake fluid flush on the Alfa Romeo Stelvio, with the same process applicable to the Giulia (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLftfWIJIWQ).\n\nAdditionally, another video provides specific steps on replacing the rear brake pads and rotors on an Alfa Romeo Stelvio Quadrifoglio (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VHTnQ6o1fNE).\n\n## Key Brake Service Mode Information\n\nThe Alfa Romeo Stelvio and Giulia share a Giorgio-platform electric parking brake (EPB) where the rear caliper doubles as the parking-brake clamp, driven by a motor and spindle, and you must wind these motors fully open first using Brake Service Mode to fit new rear pads.\n\nTo enter Brake Service Mode, open the infotainment screen settings, go to Passive Safety (or the brakes/service section) and select Brake Service Mode.\n\n## Brake Fluid Flush Procedure\n\nYou should enter Brake Service Mode via the Infotainment system, which retracts the parking brake, and suck out as much fluid from the reservoir as possible, dump a complete bottle (1L) into a clean power bleeder, and bleed brakes in the order: FL-inner, FL-outer, FR-inner, FR-outer, RR, RL.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ab76cb09-8fd0-4446-b034-2abe90e6ec51","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:11.626Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio brake fluid flush EPB service mode youtube","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01G9tLiLwTBNbu37PdysoFAr","content":[{"title":"2018-2022 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0 brake fluid flush service - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLftfWIJIWQ"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio/Giulia Quadrifoglio Brake Service Mode and Replacement- Step-By-Step - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VHTnQ6o1fNE"},{"title":"Brakes stuck in service mode!","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/brakes-stuck-in-service-mode.20545/"},{"title":"Brake fluid flush","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-fluid-flush.42916/"},{"title":"Brake fluid change","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-fluid-change.63954/"},{"title":"Brake Flush Requirements and Questions","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/brake-flush-requirements-and-questions.65821/"},{"title":"How to release stuck E-brake in Brake Service Mode","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-release-stuck-e-brake-in-brake-service-mode.50188/"},{"title":"When to replace brake fluid?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/when-to-replace-brake-fluid.18250/"},{"title":"How to Put the Electronic Parking Brake into Service Mode on a Alfa Romeo Stelvio (2017–present)","url":"https://servicereset.net/maintenance/alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-present-epb-service-mode/"},{"title":"Has anyone had a break fluid change done?","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/has-anyone-had-a-break-fluid-change-done.44588/"}]},"I found several relevant results for your search about Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio brake fluid flush and EPB service mode:\n\n## YouTube Videos\n\nThere is a step-by-step YouTube video that provides instructions on how to perform a brake fluid flush on the Alfa Romeo Stelvio, with the same process applicable to the Giulia (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PLftfWIJIWQ).\n\nAdditionally, another video provides specific steps on replacing the rear brake pads and rotors on an Alfa Romeo Stelvio Quadrifoglio (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VHTnQ6o1fNE).\n\n## Key Brake Service Mode Information\n\nThe Alfa Romeo Stelvio and Giulia share a Giorgio-platform electric parking brake (EPB) where the rear caliper doubles as the parking-brake clamp, driven by a motor and spindle, and you must wind these motors fully open first using Brake Service Mode to fit new rear pads.\n\nTo enter Brake Service Mode, open the infotainment screen settings, go to Passive Safety (or the brakes/service section) and select Brake Service Mode.\n\n## Brake Fluid Flush Procedure\n\nYou should enter Brake Service Mode via the Infotainment system, which retracts the parking brake, and suck out as much fluid from the reservoir as possible, dump a complete bottle (1L) into a clean power bleeder, and bleed brakes in the order: FL-inner, FL-outer, FR-inner, FR-outer, RR, RL."],"durationSeconds":7.460598799943924,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae332e35-71f5-4720-baf7-5a627777db3b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"67d0ea82-4529-4d39-a736-9ca239199957","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AoJupWD6nWw43mBfQspPLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Stelvio Q4 transfer case fluid change youtube forum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Transfer Case Fluid Change - AudiWorld Forums\",\"url\":\"https://www.audiworld.com/forums/q5-sq5-mkii-discussion-218/transfer-case-fluid-change-3078371/\"},{\"title\":\"Transfer case and diffs oil change Q4 advice\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/transfer-case-and-diffs-oil-change-q4-advice.67226/\"},{\"title\":\"Differential Fluid change - 2.2 diesel 210hp Q4\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/differential-fluid-change-2-2-diesel-210hp-q4.19065/\"},{\"title\":\"Stelvio 2.2 4x4 - Transfer Case Leak\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/stelvio-2-2-4x4-transfer-case-leak.1215443/\"},{\"title\":\"Oil Pump Solenoid Problems Continue\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/oil-pump-solenoid-problems-continue.19544/\"},{\"title\":\"Transmission flush\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/transmission-flush.20947/\"},{\"title\":\"All the fluids not mentioned in the manual (Differential Oil, Transfer Case Oil, & Transmission Oil).\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/all-the-fluids-not-mentioned-in-the-manual-differential-oil-transfer-case-oil-transmission-oil.20134/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Gulia/Stelvio transmission service - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PcCrAYIjLTU\"},{\"title\":\"Scotty Kilmer Checking out my Alfa Romeo Stelvio!\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/scotty-kilmer-checking-out-my-alfa-romeo-stelvio.21950/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for \"Stelvio Q4 transfer case fluid change youtube forum.\" Here are the results:\n\nThe search found several relevant resources discussing transfer case fluid changes for the Alfa Romeo Stelvio Q4:\n\n**Forum Discussions:**\n\n1. **Stelvio Forum** - There are discussions about changing fluid to differentials and the Q4 system, with mentions of AWD System FAD transfer case and AWD System TRANSFER CASE.\n\n2. **Giulia Forums** - A member performed a Power Down Calibration on a Magna Q4 Transfer Case using MES (MultiEcuScan). One user reported using Mopar 75w-85 gear oil in the rear differential and Triax 75W-80 GL4 in the transfer case, though the proper fluid for the transfer case is believed to be straight 75W gear oil.\n\n3. **Maintenance Intervals** - Recommendations suggest changing differential oil and transfer case oil at around 30-40K miles depending on driving conditions.\n\n**YouTube Content:**\n\nWhile the search did return a YouTube result about transmission service, it focuses on the ZF8HP50 transmission rather than the transfer case specifically.\n\n**Fluid Type Questions:**\n\nThere is some uncertainty about whether the OEM transfer case fluid is GL-4 or GL-5, and straight 75W gear oil can be difficult to find in the US market, though some have found aftermarket options like Motorex GL-4 transmission fluid.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1b3aaa71-7653-4fbd-b951-e3c1468ffd6e","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:12.126Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Stelvio Q4 transfer case fluid change youtube forum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01S9EodsxttJ6W1cUoFB8GFk","content":[{"title":"Transfer Case Fluid Change - AudiWorld Forums","url":"https://www.audiworld.com/forums/q5-sq5-mkii-discussion-218/transfer-case-fluid-change-3078371/"},{"title":"Transfer case and diffs oil change Q4 advice","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/transfer-case-and-diffs-oil-change-q4-advice.67226/"},{"title":"Differential Fluid change - 2.2 diesel 210hp Q4","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/differential-fluid-change-2-2-diesel-210hp-q4.19065/"},{"title":"Stelvio 2.2 4x4 - Transfer Case Leak","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/stelvio-2-2-4x4-transfer-case-leak.1215443/"},{"title":"Oil Pump Solenoid Problems Continue","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/oil-pump-solenoid-problems-continue.19544/"},{"title":"Transmission flush","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/transmission-flush.20947/"},{"title":"All the fluids not mentioned in the manual (Differential Oil, Transfer Case Oil, & Transmission Oil).","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/all-the-fluids-not-mentioned-in-the-manual-differential-oil-transfer-case-oil-transmission-oil.20134/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Gulia/Stelvio transmission service - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PcCrAYIjLTU"},{"title":"Scotty Kilmer Checking out my Alfa Romeo Stelvio!","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/scotty-kilmer-checking-out-my-alfa-romeo-stelvio.21950/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"}]},"I've completed the web search for \"Stelvio Q4 transfer case fluid change youtube forum.\" Here are the results:\n\nThe search found several relevant resources discussing transfer case fluid changes for the Alfa Romeo Stelvio Q4:\n\n**Forum Discussions:**\n\n1. **Stelvio Forum** - There are discussions about changing fluid to differentials and the Q4 system, with mentions of AWD System FAD transfer case and AWD System TRANSFER CASE.\n\n2. **Giulia Forums** - A member performed a Power Down Calibration on a Magna Q4 Transfer Case using MES (MultiEcuScan). One user reported using Mopar 75w-85 gear oil in the rear differential and Triax 75W-80 GL4 in the transfer case, though the proper fluid for the transfer case is believed to be straight 75W gear oil.\n\n3. **Maintenance Intervals** - Recommendations suggest changing differential oil and transfer case oil at around 30-40K miles depending on driving conditions.\n\n**YouTube Content:**\n\nWhile the search did return a YouTube result about transmission service, it focuses on the ZF8HP50 transmission rather than the transfer case specifically.\n\n**Fluid Type Questions:**\n\nThere is some uncertainty about whether the OEM transfer case fluid is GL-4 or GL-5, and straight 75W gear oil can be difficult to find in the US market, though some have found aftermarket options like Motorex GL-4 transmission fluid."],"durationSeconds":7.368648499965667,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"67d0ea82-4529-4d39-a736-9ca239199957","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c51ec388-a68a-430f-bd54-cad79e405661","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WeHZvYszCSbXSxBzWpP1UG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio 12V AGM battery replacement registration forum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AGM batteries\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/agm-batteries.19547/\"},{\"title\":\"Stelvio 12v Battery Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/stelvio-12v-battery-replacement.1222865/\"},{\"title\":\"What's the consensus on AGM batteries on the Stelvio/Giulia platform?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/whats-the-consensus-on-agm-batteries-on-the-stelvio-giulia-platform.25418/\"},{\"title\":\"Battery\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/battery.24701/\"},{\"title\":\"Register Battery Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/register-battery-replacement.19649/\"},{\"title\":\"Battery Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/battery-replacement.21475/\"},{\"title\":\"AGM Battery Swap and Codes?\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/agm-battery-swap-and-codes.13694/\"},{\"title\":\"AGM battery now standard replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/agm-battery-now-standard-replacement.9255/\"},{\"title\":\"Battery upgrade\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/battery-upgrade.16485/\"}]\n\nI've found several relevant discussions from Alfa Romeo owner forums regarding 12V AGM battery replacement for the Giulia and Stelvio models. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Forum Resources Found\n\nThe Alfa Romeo Stelvio Forum has active discussions about AGM batteries, with multiple threads addressing this topic. The Alfa Owner Club also hosts discussions about Stelvio 12v battery replacement.\n\n## Key Discussion Points\n\n**AGM Battery Compatibility:**\nMany posts claim replacing the OEM EFB with an AGM battery solved battery drain issues, while others claim the IBS (especially on pre-facelift models) are not programmed properly for AGM batteries and had to switch back to EFB.\n\n**Registration/Configuration:**\nStelvios and Giulias do not have a \"Register Battery Replacement\" function using a scanner.\n\n**Practical Installation Advice:**\nOne forum member reported changing a Giulia's battery successfully, only requiring steering lock-to-lock operation after the change.\n\nThe main forums where you can find these discussions are:\n- **stelvioforum.com** - dedicated Stelvio and Giulia forums\n- **alfaowner.com** - general Alfa Romeo owner community\n\nThese forums contain detailed threads with user experiences about AGM battery replacements, specific model recommendations, and troubleshooting procedures.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cafbe71e-42e6-410a-9c0c-a3721d86c540","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:13.538Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio 12V AGM battery replacement registration forum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014rpFh2W1M5Br9gLCH1iL8b","content":[{"title":"AGM batteries","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/agm-batteries.19547/"},{"title":"Stelvio 12v Battery Replacement","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/stelvio-12v-battery-replacement.1222865/"},{"title":"What's the consensus on AGM batteries on the Stelvio/Giulia platform?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/whats-the-consensus-on-agm-batteries-on-the-stelvio-giulia-platform.25418/"},{"title":"Battery","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/battery.24701/"},{"title":"Register Battery Replacement","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/register-battery-replacement.19649/"},{"title":"Battery Replacement","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/battery-replacement.21475/"},{"title":"AGM Battery Swap and Codes?","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/agm-battery-swap-and-codes.13694/"},{"title":"AGM battery now standard replacement","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/agm-battery-now-standard-replacement.9255/"},{"title":"Battery upgrade","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/battery-upgrade.16485/"}]},"I've found several relevant discussions from Alfa Romeo owner forums regarding 12V AGM battery replacement for the Giulia and Stelvio models. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Forum Resources Found\n\nThe Alfa Romeo Stelvio Forum has active discussions about AGM batteries, with multiple threads addressing this topic. The Alfa Owner Club also hosts discussions about Stelvio 12v battery replacement.\n\n## Key Discussion Points\n\n**AGM Battery Compatibility:**\nMany posts claim replacing the OEM EFB with an AGM battery solved battery drain issues, while others claim the IBS (especially on pre-facelift models) are not programmed properly for AGM batteries and had to switch back to EFB.\n\n**Registration/Configuration:**\nStelvios and Giulias do not have a \"Register Battery Replacement\" function using a scanner.\n\n**Practical Installation Advice:**\nOne forum member reported changing a Giulia's battery successfully, only requiring steering lock-to-lock operation after the change.\n\nThe main forums where you can find these discussions are:\n- **stelvioforum.com** - dedicated Stelvio and Giulia forums\n- **alfaowner.com** - general Alfa Romeo owner community\n\nThese forums contain detailed threads with user experiences about AGM battery replacements, specific model recommendations, and troubleshooting procedures."],"durationSeconds":7.8337569999694825,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c51ec388-a68a-430f-bd54-cad79e405661","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"ca8530fd-ecf7-4f12-b337-5df066ee46c2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D1PPH7DLqUBwbP5G47SNtX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ZF 8HP transmission fluid change Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio youtube forum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How-To: ZF 8HP50 and 8HP75 Transmission Fluid and Filter Change, Scan Data Information\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-zf-8hp50-and-8hp75-transmission-fluid-and-filter-change-scan-data-information.57695/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"},{\"title\":\"Transmission Fluid Recommendations ? 2.0 Petrol 8 speed.\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/transmission-fluid-recommendations-2-0-petrol-8-speed.49420/\"},{\"title\":\"All the fluids not mentioned in the manual (Differential Oil, Transfer Case Oil, & Transmission Oil).\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/all-the-fluids-not-mentioned-in-the-manual-differential-oil-transfer-case-oil-transmission-oil.20134/\"},{\"title\":\"2017-2025 Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0L AWD ZF 8HP50 Transmission: Problems, Identification, and Used Replacement\",\"url\":\"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/transmission-assembly-alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2025\"},{\"title\":\"Mode d'emploi: Changement du liquide et du filtre de transmission ZF 8HP50 et 8HP75, informations sur les données de numérisation\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-zf-8hp50-and-8hp75-transmission-fluid-and-filter-change-scan-data-information.57695/page-6?tl=fr\"},{\"title\":\"8HP ATF (FEBI BILSTEIN) 5L -Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio All\",\"url\":\"https://shop.alfissimo.com/gear-oilautomatic-transmission-fluid/2734-8hp-atf-febi-bilstein-5l-alfa-romeo-giulia-stelvio-all-.html\"},{\"title\":\"Transmission flush\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/transmission-flush.20947/\"},{\"title\":\"Transmission fluid\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/transmission-fluid.41048/\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about ZF 8HP transmission fluid changes for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here are the key findings from forums and guides:\n\n## Service Information\n\nYou will need 6 liters of fluid for a change, 7 to be safe when performing this service.\n\n## Recommended Fluids\n\nOriginal ZF fluid, ROWE 9008 ATF (ZF oil supplier/specific to 8HP) or Motul ATF VI are available. Other options include ZF Lifeguard 8 / Mopar 8&9 Speed ATF.\n\n## Service Intervals\n\nZF recommends fluid changes (drain and fill) at 60k to 90k miles. They expressly forbid flushes.\n\n## Procedure Details\n\nThe trans is filled with a plug on the side of the unit and it must be checked at a certain temperature to determine the correct fill point. You would need access to a scan tool and the trans data to do it correctly, and a lift is needed or it has to be jacked up equally on all 4 corners.\n\n## Available Resources\n\nThere's a detailed how-to guide on **giuliaforums.com** titled \"How-To: ZF 8HP50 and 8HP75 Transmission Fluid and Filter Change, Scan Data Information\" which includes ZF's official procedures and tips for both FWD and AWD models.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1f86f9d1-c6f4-4a47-ba7c-cd7bb85cc9e3","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:14.083Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"ZF 8HP transmission fluid change Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio youtube forum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Uxa9sxew4kQpDy5VYDPb6b","content":[{"title":"How-To: ZF 8HP50 and 8HP75 Transmission Fluid and Filter Change, Scan Data Information","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-zf-8hp50-and-8hp75-transmission-fluid-and-filter-change-scan-data-information.57695/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"},{"title":"Transmission Fluid Recommendations ? 2.0 Petrol 8 speed.","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/transmission-fluid-recommendations-2-0-petrol-8-speed.49420/"},{"title":"All the fluids not mentioned in the manual (Differential Oil, Transfer Case Oil, & Transmission Oil).","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/all-the-fluids-not-mentioned-in-the-manual-differential-oil-transfer-case-oil-transmission-oil.20134/"},{"title":"2017-2025 Alfa Romeo Giulia & Stelvio 2.0L AWD ZF 8HP50 Transmission: Problems, Identification, and Used Replacement","url":"https://www.go-parts.com/garage/transmission-assembly-alfa-romeo-giulia-alfa-romeo-stelvio-2017-2025"},{"title":"Mode d'emploi: Changement du liquide et du filtre de transmission ZF 8HP50 et 8HP75, informations sur les données de numérisation","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-zf-8hp50-and-8hp75-transmission-fluid-and-filter-change-scan-data-information.57695/page-6?tl=fr"},{"title":"8HP ATF (FEBI BILSTEIN) 5L -Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio All","url":"https://shop.alfissimo.com/gear-oilautomatic-transmission-fluid/2734-8hp-atf-febi-bilstein-5l-alfa-romeo-giulia-stelvio-all-.html"},{"title":"Transmission flush","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/transmission-flush.20947/"},{"title":"Transmission fluid","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/transmission-fluid.41048/"}]},"I found comprehensive information about ZF 8HP transmission fluid changes for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio vehicles. Here are the key findings from forums and guides:\n\n## Service Information\n\nYou will need 6 liters of fluid for a change, 7 to be safe when performing this service.\n\n## Recommended Fluids\n\nOriginal ZF fluid, ROWE 9008 ATF (ZF oil supplier/specific to 8HP) or Motul ATF VI are available. Other options include ZF Lifeguard 8 / Mopar 8&9 Speed ATF.\n\n## Service Intervals\n\nZF recommends fluid changes (drain and fill) at 60k to 90k miles. They expressly forbid flushes.\n\n## Procedure Details\n\nThe trans is filled with a plug on the side of the unit and it must be checked at a certain temperature to determine the correct fill point. You would need access to a scan tool and the trans data to do it correctly, and a lift is needed or it has to be jacked up equally on all 4 corners.\n\n## Available Resources\n\nThere's a detailed how-to guide on **giuliaforums.com** titled \"How-To: ZF 8HP50 and 8HP75 Transmission Fluid and Filter Change, Scan Data Information\" which includes ZF's official procedures and tips for both FWD and AWD models."],"durationSeconds":7.386580000042915,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca8530fd-ecf7-4f12-b337-5df066ee46c2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"1813fbdf-da22-41c7-a242-e8c89bd11ca6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1812edd3-f8bc-4768-a948-8fb9b39ae280","agentId":"a5dce2e7e4b866ce8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017NSDr3jfXZbpbQFcd8jkq9","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio TPMS reset relearn youtube forum\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"TPM resetting\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/tpm-resetting.60648/\"},{\"title\":\"TPMS issue\",\"url\":\"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/tpms-issue.9137/\"},{\"title\":\"How to reset tyre pressure warning?\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-reset-tyre-pressure-warning.42476/\"},{\"title\":\"Tire Pressure Monitor Warning Light Reset\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/tire-pressure-monitor-warning-light-reset.17369/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Reset Tire Pressure on an Alfa Romeo Giulia - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/aZozbSTK_ec\"},{\"title\":\"TPMS ReLearn Procedure\",\"url\":\"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/tpms-relearn-procedure.64803/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo - LEARN ABOUT TPMS\",\"url\":\"https://tpmsreset.com/category/alfa-romeo-tpms-reset-guides/\"},{\"title\":\"Tyre pressure warning reset?\",\"url\":\"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/tyre-pressure-warning-reset.1209989/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Reset and Relearn the TPMS on Your Alfa Romeo\",\"url\":\"https://erwinsalarda.com/how-to-reset-and-relearn-the-tpms-on-your-alfa-romeo/\"},{\"title\":\"Alfa Romeo Stelvio\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio\"}]\n\nI found relevant search results for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio TPMS reset and relearn procedures from both forums and a YouTube source. Here's what I found:\n\n## Forum Discussions\n\nFrom the Giulia Forums, there are multiple discussions about TPMS resetting in the Alfa Romeo Giulia. According to forum discussions, the Giulia will correctly detect the location and pressure of tires, even after rotation, but can take up to 20 minutes of driving to do so.\n\nOne forum user discussed purchasing new TPMS sensors (Huf Intellisense) for their 2018 Giulia QV and noted that a relearn is required after installation. The TPMS transmits data but can receive 125MHz pings back from the receiver—when relearning after replacement or tire rotations, the receiver pings the TPMS and receives data back like the serial number and tire pressure, which is then programmed into the car.\n\n## YouTube Video\n\nThere is a YouTube video that discusses how to reset tire pressure on an Alfa Romeo Giulia equipped with a TPMS system.\n\n## General Reset Procedure\n\nA comprehensive reset procedure involves ensuring all tires are inflated to proper pressure, parking and turning the ignition to ON without starting, navigating to the \"Car Settings\" menu using steering wheel buttons, scrolling to and selecting \"TPMS\", then selecting \"Reset Tire Pressure\".\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"298b0684-98da-4462-bf7f-ae3cf20fd35a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T01:25:14.845Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Alfa Romeo Giulia Stelvio TPMS reset relearn youtube forum","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CZGZoL9aP7dpXZ1XWo9YZe","content":[{"title":"TPM resetting","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/tpm-resetting.60648/"},{"title":"TPMS issue","url":"https://www.stelvioforum.com/threads/tpms-issue.9137/"},{"title":"How to reset tyre pressure warning?","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/how-to-reset-tyre-pressure-warning.42476/"},{"title":"Tire Pressure Monitor Warning Light Reset","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/tire-pressure-monitor-warning-light-reset.17369/"},{"title":"How to Reset Tire Pressure on an Alfa Romeo Giulia - YouTube","url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/aZozbSTK_ec"},{"title":"TPMS ReLearn Procedure","url":"https://www.giuliaforums.com/threads/tpms-relearn-procedure.64803/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo - LEARN ABOUT TPMS","url":"https://tpmsreset.com/category/alfa-romeo-tpms-reset-guides/"},{"title":"Tyre pressure warning reset?","url":"https://www.alfaowner.com/threads/tyre-pressure-warning-reset.1209989/"},{"title":"How to Reset and Relearn the TPMS on Your Alfa Romeo","url":"https://erwinsalarda.com/how-to-reset-and-relearn-the-tpms-on-your-alfa-romeo/"},{"title":"Alfa Romeo Stelvio","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Stelvio"}]},"I found relevant search results for Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio TPMS reset and relearn procedures from both forums and a YouTube source. Here's what I found:\n\n## Forum Discussions\n\nFrom the Giulia Forums, there are multiple discussions about TPMS resetting in the Alfa Romeo Giulia. According to forum discussions, the Giulia will correctly detect the location and pressure of tires, even after rotation, but can take up to 20 minutes of driving to do so.\n\nOne forum user discussed purchasing new TPMS sensors (Huf Intellisense) for their 2018 Giulia QV and noted that a relearn is required after installation. The TPMS transmits data but can receive 125MHz pings back from the receiver—when relearning after replacement or tire rotations, the receiver pings the TPMS and receives data back like the serial number and tire pressure, which is then programmed into the car.\n\n## YouTube Video\n\nThere is a YouTube video that discusses how to reset tire pressure on an Alfa Romeo Giulia equipped with a TPMS system.\n\n## General Reset Procedure\n\nA comprehensive reset procedure involves ensuring all tires are inflated to proper pressure, parking and turning the ignition to ON without starting, navigating to the \"Car Settings\" menu using steering wheel buttons, scrolling to and selecting \"TPMS\", then selecting \"Reset Tire Pressure\"."],"durationSeconds":8.59407690000534,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"02c416c2-f0b0-4eac-8cfa-525d44c4c844","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/User/mcp-servers","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1813fbdf-da22-41c7-a242-e8c89bd11ca6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
